<title>RUSSIA: Rouble firms on short-covering, after Tbill sales.</title>
<headline>Rouble firms on short-covering, after Tbill sales.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian rouble firmed in active trading on Friday, as dealers sought to cover short positions, dealers said.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Apr 4 midday   Apr 4 early    Apr 3 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,737-38	 5,742-43	 5,740-42</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,738-39	 5,741-42	 5,741-42</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)   15-20	     5-7		5-10</p>
<p>			   Apr 4				 Apr 3</p>
<p> central bank	  5,730/44			    5,728/42</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,739				 5,741</p>
<p>&quot;The rouble firmed as banks got overdosed with dollars yesterday.&quot; an SBS-Agro Bank dealer said. &quot;Also, they were short of roubles after active investing in Treasury bills (on Thursday).&quot;</p>
<p>ABN-Amro Bank dealer Artur Lotov said banks were fulfilling client orders to buy roubles and said he saw some non-resident demand for roubles to buy T-bills.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
